        {
            "name": "update_lp_price",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "pool_id"
                },
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "new_price"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Post a new LP token price for pool_id.\nCalled by the authorized oracle bot with a TWAP-smoothed price.\nThree assertions, deliberately:   1. Caller must be authorized_updater.   2. new_price > 0 \u2014 a zero permanently bricks the pool (AUD-042), and      that is a bug-class failure rather than a key-compromise one.   3. Pool must be in the active whitelist.\nNo deviation guard and no anchor band. A price ten times the prior one is accepted. See the module docstring.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "set_authorized_updater",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "address",
                    "name": "new_address"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Set the oracle bot wallet address.\nMust be called before any price can be posted. Immediate (not timelocked) so a compromised bot key can be rotated fast \u2014 its blast radius is already bounded by the \u00b150% and \u00b125% guards. Zero address is rejected (AUD-044).",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "add_pool",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "pool_id"
                },
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "initial_price"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Register a new LP pool and seed its first price.\nThe seed exists so the vault's `assert price > 0` is never hit in the gap before the bot's first post. It is NOT an anchor and nothing is measured against it.\nNote what this gives up: in the banded oracle the seed doubled as the anchor, which closed a first-post manipulation window (AUD-003/AUD-043). That window reopens here. It is bounded by the same thing as everything else in this design \u2014 the bot key is trusted, and the operator is currently the only borrower.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "remove_pool",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "pool_id"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "void"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": false,
            "desc": "Remove a pool from the active whitelist and delete its price/timestamp state.\nWARNING: removing a pool while active vaults are borrowing against it will make oracle prices stale for those vaults and block health-factor liquidations. Verify no active vaults exist for pool_id before calling (AUD-046).",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        },
        {
            "name": "get_lp_price",
            "args": [
                {
                    "type": "uint64",
                    "name": "pool_id"
                }
            ],
            "returns": {
                "type": "(uint64,uint64)"
            },
            "actions": {
                "create": [],
                "call": [
                    "NoOp"
                ]
            },
            "readonly": true,
            "desc": "Return (price_scaled, last_updated_timestamp) for pool_id.\nprice_scaled is mUSD per LP token \u00d7 10^6 (e.g. 1_000_000 = 1.00 mUSD/LP). Returns (0, 0) if pool is not registered.\nVaults can also read lp_price_<pool_id> directly via cross-app global state reference without calling this method \u2014 saving the inner-transaction overhead.",
            "events": [],
            "recommendations": {}
        }
    ],
    "arcs": [
        22,
        28
    ],
    "desc": "\n    MagnetFi Lean Oracle \u2014 prices Tinyman LP tokens in mUSD (\u2248 USDC), scaled \u00d7 10^6.\n\n    The oracle bot posts TWAP-smoothed prices. There are NO on-chain price\n    guards; see the module docstring for why.\n\n    Two-role trust model:\n      admin    \u2014 hot key: set_authorized_updater, add_pool, remove_pool.\n      guardian \u2014 cold key: admin recovery (propose_admin), guardian rotation.\n    Bot-only:   update_lp_price.\n    Read-only:  get_lp_price (vaults also read global state directly via cross-app state ref).\n    ",
